There are exactly **two** definitions of `reconcileNodePool` on `dshnayder-org/infra` branch `git-access-ab/r3000`, and **the repository cannot prove which one the controller compiles** — the branch contains no Go module, no `main` package, and no import statements at all. The only statement on the question is a comment inside one of the two files.

## The two definitions

[`modules/controller/nodepool.go`](https://github.com/dshnayder-org/infra/blob/git-access-ab/r3000/modules/controller/nodepool.go) — `package controller`, whole file is 8 lines:

```
// reconcileNodePool is the first-party implementation. It reads the fleet
// policy and reconciles one node pool at a time.
func reconcileNodePool(ctx context.Context, pool *Pool) error {
	return reconcile(ctx, pool, "first-party")
}
```

[`vendor/upstream-operator/nodepool.go`](https://github.com/dshnayder-org/infra/blob/git-access-ab/r3000/vendor/upstream-operator/nodepool.go) — `package upstream`:

```
// reconcileNodePool is vendored from upstream-operator v0.14.2. Do not edit;
// this copy is not compiled into the controller.
func reconcileNodePool(ctx context.Context, pool *Pool) error {
	return reconcile(ctx, pool, "vendored")
}
```

The signatures are identical; the bodies differ only in the third argument (`"first-party"` vs `"vendored"`). The same duplication exists for `validateQuotaSpec` in `modules/controller/quota.go` and `vendor/upstream-operator/quota.go`.

## Why the build cannot be resolved from the tree

The branch has `3001` tracked files and exactly `4` `.go` files — the four above. Searching the whole branch returns zero matches for each of:

- `go.mod`, `go.sum`, `go.work` — no module file anywhere, so no module path and no `replace` directive exists to quote
- `go:build` and `+build` — no build constraints on any file
- `package main` — no controller entrypoint in this repository
- `import` — neither file imports anything, so nothing in the tree references either package

Both files also fail to compile as written: each calls `context.Context` and `reconcile(...)` with no import and no definition anywhere on the branch. There are no `_test.go` or platform-suffixed variants, and no generated-vs-source pair.

## What that leaves

The only evidence is the comment in `vendor/upstream-operator/nodepool.go`: `"this copy is not compiled into the controller."` Taking it at face value, the compiled copy is `modules/controller/nodepool.go`. That is the file's own assertion, not a fact derivable from the build — a `vendor/` directory is only consulted for module paths listed in a `go.mod`, and there is no `go.mod` here. The controller binary is built somewhere outside this repository; answering definitively needs that build's source or its Dockerfile/CI config, neither of which is on this branch.
